    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to present this traditional detached cottage extending to approximately 142.46 sq.m (1,533 sq.ft.), occupying a mature countryside setting just minutes from Oughterard Village. Rich in character and original features, this appealing property presents an increasingly rare opportunity to restore and transform a traditional Irish home in one of County Galway's most sought-after locations.Set behind traditional stone boundary walls the property immediately conveys a wonderful sense of character and history. The property's convenient location provides easy access to Oughterard Village, Oughterard Golf Course, Lough Corrib and the many fantastic amenities the area has to offer. Internally, the residence retains many traditional features synonymous with homes of its era, including a striking inglenook fireplace with solid fuel stove, original staircase, decorative fireplaces and generously proportioned accommodation. While the property requires extensive refurbishment throughout, it offers purchasers a superb opportunity to restore and modernise a home of genuine character while preserving its original charm and heritage.Complementing the residence is a substantial detached two-storey stone outbuilding, providing valuable storage together with exciting potential for workshop space, hobby use or future conversion, subject to the necessary planning permission.The location is one of the property's greatest strengths. Oughterard, renowned as the Gateway to Connemara, is only a short drive away and offers an excellent range of cafés, restaurants, shops, schools and everyday amenities. Oughterard Golf Club is within easy reach, while the renowned waters of Lough Corrib, famous for their trout and salmon fishing, boating and lakeside recreation, are nearby. The surrounding area offers exceptional opportunities for walking, cycling and exploring the spectacular landscapes of Connemara, while Galway City is approximately a 30-minute drive away.The property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, together with a range of Sustainable Energy Authority of Ireland (SEAI) energy efficiency grants, subject to the relevant eligibility criteria and approval. These schemes provide an excellent opportunity for purchasers undertaking refurbishment works to restore and enhance this traditional home.Traditional properties of this nature are becoming increasingly difficult to find. Combining original character, mature surroundings, an excellent location and exceptional restoration potential, this delightful cottage offers purchasers the opportunity to create a truly distinctive home in one of the West of Ireland's most desirable settings.Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the character, setting and exceptional potential this unique property has to offer."
      },
